tests/full/hv_reset -- the hypervisor (q.bin / reset.bin) gate, GNU path
========================================================================

Checks on the GNU-built hypervisor that need no Sun build, no Solaris host and
no QEMU:

    make hv-verify        build once (ontario/legion by default), run all;
                          about 10 s

They exist because build/hv_reset/gnu/build.sh is a port, and GNU as does not
always mean by a source what Sun as means. Each test is the cheapest check that
would have caught a difference found by comparing a GNU build with a build by
Sun's toolchain, function by function.

Layout
------
    run                     runs internal/*.sh in order, stops at the first
                            failure
    internal/
      no-asm-warnings.sh    the build has no `Warning:` and no failed file.
                            The build script hides stderr; lib/build.sh runs
                            the same script with it visible. Catches
                            `set <negative>` (GNU sign-extends, Sun
                            zero-extends).
      setx-rd-pc.sh         every `setx <label>` followed by `rd %pc`
                            relocates to that rd's own address. Catches
                            `setx .+8` (GNU takes `.` at the start of the
                            six-instruction expansion, Sun at the end).
      offsets-cross-check.sh
                            offsets.h computed two independent ways agrees
                            (the build's DWARF reader, and lib/genoffsets.py
                            where gcc evaluates offsetof/sizeof itself), and
                            for ontario/legion offsets.h and offsets.chk are
                            byte-identical to the Sun-made gnu/reference/.
                            Catches a DWARF reader that misreads a layout.
    lib/build.sh            the shared build, stderr visible; reused if OUTDIR
                            already holds one
    lib/genoffsets.py       the second, independent computation of offsets.h
                            (the build no longer uses it)

What this does NOT cover
------------------------
Only ontario/legion is meant to pass: the release and debug variants do not
link under the GNU path (with CONFIG_FIRE/PCIE, -traditional-cpp rejects macros
in vpci_errs.h), so `make hv-verify PLATFORM=ontario VARIANT=release` fails in
the build, not in a test (on the command line: set in the environment, the value is
overridden by build/hv_reset/options.mk and the legion build runs instead). Nothing here compares against Sun's output, the C
half (gcc vs Sun cc), the link layout, or run-time behaviour. The full
comparison needs a build with Sun's toolchain; the tools for it are not in this
repository.

Adding a test
-------------
Drop an executable internal/<name>.sh that builds through lib/build.sh, exits
non-zero on failure, and prints one `ok:` line on success; add the name to
ORDER in `run`. Say in its header what it catches, and show it failing on a
tree that has the defect -- otherwise nobody knows it can.
